✅ Day 2: Advanced File Management & File Permissions

🎯 Goals:

Learn about file permissions (read, write, execute)

Understand chmod, chown, and chgrp commands

Practice hidden files and file viewing commands

📂 1. File Permissions Basics
Har file/directory ka ek permission hota hai:

ls -l

Example:

-rwxr-xr--  1 user group 4096 Apr 8 10:30 script.sh
Breakdown:

-: file type (- for file, d for directory)

rwx: Owner permissions

r-x: Group permissions

r--: Others permissions

🔧 2. Changing Permissions – chmod
Symbolic mode:


chmod u+x file.sh      # user ko execute permission do
chmod g-w file.txt     # group se write permission hatao
chmod o+r file.txt     # others ko read permission do

Numeric mode:

Symbol	Value
r	4
w	2
x	1

Total example:

chmod 755 file.sh → Owner = rwx (7), Group = r-x (5), Others = r-x (5)

3. Change Ownership – chown

sudo chown newuser:newgroup file.txt

🧾 4. Working with Hidden Files
Create a hidden file:

touch .hiddenfile
View hidden files:

ls -a
📘 5. View File Content

Command	              Description

cat file.txt	     View all content
more file.txt	     Page by page
less file.txt	     Scroll up/down
head -n 5 file.txt   First 5 lines
tail -n 5 file.txt   Last 5 lines

